        "Build a list of prospects that:\n- Clearly fit your service\n- Have a visible problem you can help with\n- Can plausibly afford the service\n- Have a reachable decision-maker\n- Are not already an obvious poor fit\nFor example, if you provide short-form video production, look for businesses whose products are visually demonstrable and whose current social content could be improved.\n6.2 Personalise the first message\nA good outreach message should contain:\n- A genuine observation about the business\n- A specific opportunity or problem\n- A concise description of your relevant capability\n- A relevant example or portfolio link\n- A low-friction next step\nAvoid generic blasts, false compliments, fake urgency, and exaggerated promises.\nExample outreach message\nHi [Name],",
