        "Examples:\n- Ask better questions before starting.\n- Understand the client's audience and objective.\n- Plan the work carefully.\n- Communicate deadlines.\n- Share progress when useful.\n- Check the work before delivery.\n- Make the handover easy.\n- Offer a concise recommendation for the next step.\n7.2 Use a project brief\nBefore beginning, document:\n- Client objective\n- Target audience\n- Scope and deliverables\n- Timeline\n- Responsibilities\n- Required assets and access\n- Approval process\n- Revision limits\n- Price and payment schedule\n- Success measures\nA written agreement reduces confusion and protects both parties.\n7.3 Turn the result into proof\nAfter delivery, ask the client for feedback and permission to use the work in your portfolio. If the work produces measurable results, request permission to describe those results accurately.",
